  "english": "Tuesday. Tone 3 [gkay]. Patristic Hymn [Harst] Tone 1 [ak]: \"Your name, O Christ\" (Zanun ko krisdos).\nMidday Liturgy Psalm 5: \"I will worship in your temple\" (Yergirpagits i dajar).\nThe Apostle: Romans 15:1 to verse 13: \"the Holy Spirit\" (hokvohn srboy).\nAlleluia: \"Sing to the Lord\" (Yergetsek dyarn).\nGospel: Matthew 15:1: \"Then came to him...\" to verse 20: \"defiles a man\" (pghdse zmart).\n\nWednesday. Tone 4 [da]. Patristic Hymn [Harst] Tone 1 [ak]: \"You who humbled yourself to our weakness\" (Or khonarhhetsar i tgarutiuns).\nMidday Liturgy Psalm 64 [65]: \"Save [me/us]\" (Ketso).\nThe Apostle: Romans 15:14: \"I myself am satisfied...\" to verse 29: \"I shall come in [the fullness of the blessing of] Christ\" (krisdosi yegits).\nAlleluia: \"Remember, O Lord, your compassion\" (Yishea der zgdutuyun).\nGospel: Matthew 15:21: \"And Jesus went away from there...\" to verse 28: \"from that very hour\" (i nmin bahu).\n\nThursday. Tone 4 [kay]. Patristic Hymn [Harst] Tone 1 [ak]: \"God of our fathers\" (Asdvadz hardsn merots).\nMidday Liturgy Psalm 98 [99]: \"Extol [the Lord]\" (Pardzr ararek).\nThe Apostle: Romans 15:30: \"I appeal to you...\" to chapter 16:10: \"[approved in] Christ\" (krisdosi).\nAlleluia: \"Extol [the Lord]\" (Pardzr ararek).\nGospel: Matthew 15:29: \"And Jesus went away from there...\" to verse 38: \"and the children\" (yev zmangdis).\n\nFriday. Tone 4 [da]. Rest Hymn [Harts Hankisdyan] Tone 3 [gk]: \"Who with glory\" (Or parok).\nMidday Liturgy Psalm 97 [98]: \"All the ends have seen\" (Desin amenayn dzakg).\nThe Apostle: Romans 16:17: \"I appeal to you...\" to verse 27: \"forever, Amen\" (yavidyans amen).\nAlleluia: \"Your Holy Spirit\" (Hoki ko surb).\nGospel: Matthew 15:39: \"And after sending away...\" to chapter 16:12: \"[yeast] of the Sadducees\" (sadugedsots).\n\nSaturday. Tone 1 [ak]. Commemoration of the Old Ark [of the Covenant], and Feast of this New Holy Church.\nHymn at Dawn [ah] Tone 1 [ak]: \"O city of God, you\" (Uzkez kaghak asdudzo), with its canons.\nMorning Song: \"Arise, O Lord, into your rest\" (Ari der i han). Verse: \"Remember, O Lord, David\" (Yishea der zdavit).\n\"Holy God\" (Surb asdvadz), who wast crucified.\nHymn of the Youth [Mangkunk] Tone 1 [ak]: \"Who from the beginning\" (Or i sgzpane).\nAfter the Youth Hymn, Litany: \"By this holy church\" (Surb yegeghetsyavs). Save [us] (Ketso).\nPrayer: \"At the door of the Holy [Temple]\" (Ar dran surb).\nMidday Liturgical Introit: \"Peace [unto all]\" (Zkhaghaghutiun).\nHymn Tone 1 [ak]: \"Who from the beginning\" (Or i sgzpane).\nPsalm 131 [132]: \"Arise, O Lord, into your rest\" (Ari der i han). Verse: \"Remember, O Lord\" (Yishea der).\nReading from Exodus 25:10: \"And the Lord said to Moses...\" to verse 14: \"the ark\" (ztabanakn).\nReading from Joshua 3:14: \"And it came to pass when...\" to chapter 4:18: \"and upon the dry land\" (yev yyerantn).\nReading from 1 Samuel 6:18: \"And they did not please...\" to chapter 7:2: \"twenty years\" (amk ksan).\nReading from 2 Samuel 6:12: \"And David went...\" to verse 19: \"to his house\" (i dun yur).\nThe Prophet Jeremiah: \"The prophet Jeremiah...\" to \"unto this day\" (This is not found in the Bible, see the Lectionary [Chashots]).\nThe Apostle: Hebrews 9:1: \"Indeed, even the first...\" to verse 10: \"were imposed\" (i veray gayin).\nAlleluia: \"Arise, O Lord\" (Ari der).\nGospel: Matthew 5:17: \"Do not think...\" to verse 20: \"the kingdom of heaven\" (arkayutiunn yergnits).\nHymn of Hallowing: \"Angelic\" (Hreshtagayin).\nIn the Evening: \"Joyous Light\" (Luys zvart).\nMessedi: \"Bless the Lord, all you...\" (Asd ohnesetsek). Verse: \"You who stand\" (O gayk).\nLitany: \"Let us say\" (Asasguk).\n\"Holy God\" (Surb asdvadz), who wast crucified.\nAnd the priests shall vest together, and they shall come out into the chancel with the cross and the Gospel and in full vestments, and they shall sing:\nHymn of Ascent [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ay]: \"Who on the mountain wast transfigured\" (Or i lerinn aylagerbyal).\nAfterwards, Litany: \"Let us ask\" (Khntresguk). Save [us] (Ketso).\nPrayer: \"O King of Peace\" (Takavor khaghaghutian).",
